remembering a loved one lost one year  later he was just a special  special guy gerard nieva's brother  donald ray says he lived and breathed  bicycles and it was something the two  shared before his life was suddenly  stolen it was pretty much his life he  would you know wake up thinking about it  go to sleep thinking about it gerard was  one of five killed on december 10 2020  when a commercial truck driver who was  high on methamphetamine swerved and hit  a group of cyclists on the u.s 95 near  searchlight we still miss them  we think about them every day shawn  tyrone who works at las vegas cyclery  says this crash really rocked the entire  community it was a very huge blow to us  i mean we all knew and love and rode  with  with the entire group he wants to make  sure these names are never forgotten and  hopes this tragedy will always serve as  a reminder we need to advocate for safer  roads for driver awareness  and not  not let this just get swept under the  rug and forgotten he and donald ray are  asking others to keep an eye out i just  think people should be more aware of  cyclists and think of gerard who loved  to travel anywhere on two wheels the  pain will always be there  briana remembrance ride will take place  tomorrow at 7 a.m we have more info on  that on our website now as for the truck  driver he was sentenced to at least 16  years in prison earlier this year  and again we will have more on that on  our website reporting live tonight sasha  loftis live local now
 

